        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0137" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg75"/>

                <head>No. 62.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williamson to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States at Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 14, 1878</date>. (Received February 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 752.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor of inclosing you a copy
                    and translation of a decree of the Government of Guatemala, just issued,
                    reducing the duty upon flour $1 per quintal, or about 1 cent per pound. The duty
                    on that article still remains very high.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. WILLIAMSON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d67-a1.xml" xpointer="d67-a1"/>
            </div>
